From 0a53fe2e352bab686106d4b303a63b4a150dda9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Hargett <plaztiksyke@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 02:22:52 -0700
Subject: cranelift/pulley: pass first 4 indirect-call args via call_indirectN
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mirror of the direct-call arg-bundling in `Inst::Call`: extend
`Inst::IndirectCall`'s `info.dest` from `XReg` to a new
`PulleyCallIndirect { target, args: SmallVec<[XReg; 4]> }` payload,
parallel to `PulleyCall`. `gen_call_ind_info` pulls the first 0–4
integer args out of `uses` (where they were going through regalloc's
`reg_fixed_use`, costing one `xmov` each) into `args`, where they
flow as free reg uses and the emitted `call_indirect{1,2,3,4}`
opcode does the move-into-x0..x3 at call time.

The emit side picks the narrowest op for the call after the same
"drop args already in their ABI register" loop that direct calls
use. With phase-3's `xband_funcref_dispatch_*` writing `dst_vmctx`
into a free register, the previously-emitted `xmov x0, dst_vmctx;
call_indirect dst_code` pair at the dispatch tail collapses to a
single `call_indirect1 dst_code, dst_vmctx` op — one fewer Pulley
dispatch per call_indirect on the lazy-init fast path. Indirect
calls with 0/2/3/4 ABI args benefit identically via the matching
`call_indirect{,2,3,4}` opcodes.

iPhone 12 A14 Icestorm wallclock (N=10, BENCH_TARGET_MS=2000,
`.utility` QoS) vs phase 3:
- vtable_poly4 −8.94%
- vtable_bi    −6.71%
- vtable_poly6 −3.72%
- xmrsplayer   −2.17%
- vtable_mono  −0.68%

Filetest snapshots updated for the new `dest` shape; no behaviour
change in the pretty-printed form. All 13 wasmtime
craneliftpulley_call_* integration tests pass.
